{
  "analysis": "uv is installed. Now I need to initialize the Reflex project. I'll create the project directory and use uv to set up the environment.",
  "plan": "1. Create /home/user/filtered_table directory\n2. Run uv init in that directory\n3. Add reflex to the environment\n4. Initialize the Reflex project with the blank template",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /home/user/filtered_table && cd /home/user/filtered_table\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv init --python 3.11 --no-readme --no-pin-python --bare\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "uv init created the project. Now I need to add reflex as a dependency.",
  "plan": "1. Add reflex to the project\n2. Initialize the reflex project with blank template",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat pyproject.toml\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv add reflex\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Reflex is installed. Now I need to initialize the Reflex project with the blank template. The current python is 3.12 not 3.11 because pyproject had requires-python = '>=3.11' but uv used 3.12. Let me run reflex init with the blank template.",
  "plan": "1. Run reflex init with blank template (using --template blank to avoid prompts)\n2. Check the project structure",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv run reflex init --template blank --no-install-deps 2>&1 | head -50\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let me check the help for reflex init to see what options are available.",
  "plan": "Check reflex init options",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv run reflex init --help\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let me run reflex init with the blank template. I should set CI=true to make it non-interactive.",
  "plan": "Run reflex init with template blank and CI=true to avoid prompts",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "CI=true uv run reflex init --template blank --no-agents 2>&1 | head -80\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Reflex project initialized. Let me check the project structure.",
  "plan": "Explore the project structure to understand what was created",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la filtered_table/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la assets/ 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat rxconfig.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat filtered_table/filtered_table.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The project structure is set up. I need to:\n1. Update rxconfig.py to set db_url and api_transformer\n2. Define the Product model\n3. Create a seeding mechanism\n4. Build the State class with filter/sort vars and background event\n5. Build the UI with debounce_input, dropdowns, etc.\n6. Add the API endpoint at /api/filter\n\nLet me first check if I need to update rxconfig.py to add db_url.",
  "plan": "I'll restructure the project: keep the app module, add a models module, and update rxconfig.py. Let me first look at what's available in the reflex library to understand the API.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv run python -c \"import reflex; print(reflex.__version__); print(reflex.__file__)\"\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let me look at the relevant reflex modules to understand the API.",
  "plan": "Check rx.Model, rx.asession, and rx.debounce_input",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv run python -c \"import reflex as rx; print(dir(rx))\" 2>&1 | head -30\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see `debounce_input`, `Model`, `asession`, `event`, etc. Let me check the signature of `debounce_input` and `Model`.",
  "plan": "Check debounce_input signature",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv run python -c \"import reflex as rx; help(rx.debounce_input)\" 2>&1 | head -40\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

